  p1Sub:'This is not a general library: it is your actual inventory, crossed against what each vendor does for you.',
  p1:[
    ['Your edge: Cloudflare (www, online)','Cloudflare enables hybrid key exchange by default, on every plan and on both legs. These two hosts already have it without you doing anything; all that is left is confirming that no restricted cipher-suite configuration in your zone is switching it off.'],
    ['api, legacy, mail — no CDN','There is no provider between your server and anyone watching, which is why they remain fully classical. What Cloudflare does or does not do never reaches them: their exposure depends entirely on what you configure.'],
  ],
  p2Tag:'Part 2', p2H:'The vendor library',
  p2Sub:'The typical vendors in your industry, with what you would have to do in each case. Every row carries its source; anything unconfirmed is declared as such.',
  trampasH:'Word traps — the same finding stated backwards',
  regH:'Regulatory framework', regJur:'Loaded jurisdiction: Chile — this block is a per-country module, not fixed text.',
  regCols:['Rule','What it establishes','Requires PQC?'],
  rwH:'Where you stand, against whom, and how much time is left',
  rwSub:'One chart, three questions. Your score (the dot), your sector’s middle half (the band), and the probability zones for the threat existing (the background, cited to the Global Risk Institute).',
  rwYou:'You, today', rwSector:'Sector middle half', rwMed:'Sector median',
  rwHoy:'today', rwFin:'~15 years', rwHitos:'the first 12 months of your roadmap',
  rwCap:'<b>No trajectory line.</b> No model exists today that computes what score results from executing the roadmap, and drawing one would be inventing data. That absence is a decision.',
  rwSrc:'Time zones: Global Risk Institute, Quantum Threat Timeline Report 2025. Sector band: Rosetta’s August 2026 study of 220 Chilean organizations.',
  s2b:'The four clocks',
  relP:'The fair objection is “no rule obliges me yet”. It is true, and it changes nothing: four clocks are running and the regulator’s is the slowest.',
  rel:[
    ['Your deadline is set by the shelf life of your data','crit','A mortgage has to stay secret for decades. Your deadline is not set by the regulator: it is set by how long your data must remain secret.'],
    ['The debt is already running','crit','Traffic leaving encrypted today may be stored now to be read later. Nothing you do in 2030 protects what left in 2026.'],
    ['The requirement reaches you by contract before it reaches you by law','warn','Your parent company, a correspondent bank or a large client’s security questionnaire will ask before any Chilean regulator does.'],
    ['The technical dates are already written','warn','NIST sets deprecation of RSA and elliptic curves at 2030 and disallowance at 2035. The document (IR 8547) is still an initial public draft and we say so: not a binding obligation, but the date your vendors plan against.'],
  ],
  chileH:'And in Chile, plainly',
  chileP:'<b>As of this report, no Chilean regulator requires post-quantum cryptography.</b> Not the CMF, not the ANCI, not the data protection agency. What does exist are operational-risk and information-security obligations under which a supervisor may ask about your plan. This report will not imply an obligation that does not exist.',
  s3:'What is good',
  good:['www and online negotiate the hybrid today because Cloudflare ships it on by default. It is neither a pending win nor a decision of yours: it is a side effect of your CDN contract, and it covers only 2 of your 5 hosts.','TLS 1.3 present on www and online; no export ciphers observed.','DMARC and SPF configured on the mail domain.'],
  s4:'What is wrong / critical', sev:'Severity', findingCol:'Finding', detailCol:'Detail',
  sevtbl:[
    ['Critical','3 of 5 hosts fully classical','api, legacy and mail do not negotiate X25519MLKEM768. The protection you do have arrives only where the CDN brings it.'],
    ['Critical','Banking HNDL, unmitigated','Long-lived data exposed under classical cryptography.'],
    ['High','TLS 1.1 + RSA-1024','legacy.acme-bank.example accepts obsolete protocols and keys.'],
    ['Medium','Wildcards + CT orphans','Wide blast radius; unmanaged surface.'],
    ['Low','No crypto-agility policy','No declared owner or rotation process.'],
  ],
  s5b:'Your critical path runs through your vendors',
  provP:'We cross the vendors visible on your surface, and the typical ones for your industry, against each manufacturer’s declared post-quantum status. This is what sets your real timeline — and it does not depend on you.',
  provCols:['Layer','Vendor','Post-quantum status','What it means for you'],
  prov:[
    ['Public edge','Cloudflare','Available and on by default','ok','Nothing to do. Already there.'],
    ['Public edge','Akamai Enhanced TLS','Available and on by default','ok','Nothing to do if your origin is on Enhanced.'],
    ['Public edge','Akamai Standard TLS','Not available at that tier','crit','A product-tier change. Contract, not engineering.'],
    ['Core banking','Temenos · Finacle · FIS · Fiserv','None has published a date','crit','The longest link, and the one you do not control. Ask them in writing now.'],
    ['Payment switch','Visa · ACI Worldwide','No public roadmap','crit','Same as above: with no vendor date there is no plan you can make.'],
    ['Payment HSM','Thales payShield','No public statement','crit','Where your keys live. Without an answer, the rest of the plan is theoretical.'],
    ['Financial messaging','Swift','July 2027 · requires Alliance 7.9','warn','There is a date. If you are on 7.7 there is no direct path: plan the jump.'],
    ['Network & VPN','Cisco ASA / Secure Client','Real ML-KEM late 2026','warn','Updating today does not fix it. Wait for the release and plan the window.'],
  ],
  provNota:'Status as declared by each manufacturer in public sources, with the date consulted. A “no date” does not mean the vendor is not working on it: it means you cannot plan against anything.',
  s5:'Observed inventory', invcols:['Host','TLS / algorithms','Hybrid','Edge'],
  inv:[
    ['www.acme-bank.example','TLS 1.3 · X25519MLKEM768 / RSA-2048','Sí · por defecto del CDN','Cloudflare'],
    ['online.acme-bank.example','TLS 1.3 · X25519MLKEM768 / RSA-2048','Sí · por defecto del CDN','Cloudflare'],
    ['api.acme-bank.example','TLS 1.2 · ECDHE / ECDSA P-256','No','—'],
    ['legacy.acme-bank.example','TLS 1.1 · RSA / RSA-1024','No','—'],
    ['mail.acme-bank.example','STARTTLS · ECDHE / RSA-2048','No','—'],
  ],
  s6:'HNDL index + CRQC scenarios', hndlP:'Banking = high confidentiality horizon. The HNDL index combines sector with observed exposure:',
  scen:[
    ['5 years · 2031','~15 %','Your migration is half done. Four years with a live threat while you migrate.','crit'],
    ['10 years · 2036','28–49 %','Your migration just finished. Everything harvested before is still readable.','crit'],
    ['15 years · 2041','≥ 51 %','Protected from then on; not what left before 2035.','warn'],
    ['20 years · 2046','≥ 69 %','Protected.','ok'],
  ],
  scenFuente:'Global Risk Institute · Quantum Threat Timeline Report 2025 (7th edition, March 2026, 26 experts). Aggregate probability that a computer able to factor 2048 bits in under 24 hours exists.',
  scenAdv:'Small sample with varying composition year to year; probability bins are not uniform. The 2019–2021 surveys gave a higher probability for the same horizon.',
  s7:'Global Q-Ready score', scoreP:'Weighted mean of the dimensions measurable at the External tier:',
  dims:ORDEN.map(k => [{cert:'Certificates / public PKI', higiene:'Surface & hygiene', hndl:'HNDL posture (time)', edge:'Edge TLS PQC'}[k], PESOS[k]+'%', String(VALORES[k])]),
  bands:leyenda(SCORE, false),
  s8:'Roadmap',
  rmCols:['Action','Effort','Cost'],
  rm:[
    ['30 days','Hygiene & visibility',[
      ['Inventory public certificates and CT hostnames','hours','no cost'],
      ['Force TLS 1.3 and disable TLS 1.1 on the legacy host','hours','no cost'],
      ['Replace the RSA-1024 certificate','hours','no cost'],
      ['Publish security.txt with a contact channel','minutes','no cost']]],
    ['90 days','Hybrid where it is missing',[
      ['Enable X25519MLKEM768 on the three hosts with no CDN (api, legacy, mail): OpenSSL 3.5+ or your server\u2019s equivalent','days','no cost'],
      ['Check that no cipher-suite restriction is disabling the hybrid Cloudflare already brings on www and online','minutes','no cost'],
      ['Consolidate wildcards and retire orphan hostnames','days','no cost'],
      ['Name a crypto-agility owner and define key rotation','days','no cost']]],
    ['365 days','Interior',[
      ['Cryptographic inventory of internal systems (CBOM)','weeks','needs budget'],
      ['Post-quantum plan with HSM and key-management vendors','weeks','needs budget'],
      ['Migrate signatures to ML-DSA where the vendor already supports it','weeks','needs budget'],
      ['Quarterly re-scan','—','subscription']]],
  ],
  rmNota:'The “no cost” actions require no purchase: they are your own team’s work with tools you already have. None of them is “flip a toggle on Cloudflare”: on hosts already behind Cloudflare the hybrid ships on by default, and there is nothing to enable.',
  s9:'Visibility gaps', gapP:'The External tier does not observe the interior. These gaps close with Assisted (uploads + integrations) and Enterprise (partner):',
  gaps:['HSM/KMS inventory and internal keys','Apps, VPN and internal mTLS','Encrypted databases and backups','Vendor PQC roadmaps'],
  gapCta:'Upgrade to Assisted →',
  s10:'Appendix · methodology & limits',
  method:'Public-surface evidence only: Certificate Transparency, DNS resolution, TLS probe (ClientHello with hybrid groups), public trust chain and light OSINT. No exploits, no aggressive port-scan, identified User-Agent. Not a certification and no substitute for a formal internal review.',
  s11:'Rosetta seal', sealP:'Each report is sealed with the hash of the evidence JSON. In production it anchors to the Evidence Ledger (here, a sample, unanchored).',
};
const sevClass = (s) => s.toLowerCase();
---
<article class="report">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="qr-cta no-print" style="justify-content:space-between;margin-top:24px">
      <a class="mono faint" href={p('/q-ready')} style="font-size:13px;align-self:center">{t.back}</a>
      <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="qr-print" type="button">{t.print}</button>
    </div>
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:22px">{t.eyebrow}</div>
    <div class="demo-tag no-print" style="margin-bottom:8px">{t.demo}</div>

    <!-- 1 · exec brief -->
    <div class="rep-head">
      <div>
        <div class="rep-meta">{t.co} · {t.dom}</div>
        <h1 class="rep-title">{t.h1}</h1>
        <div class="rep-meta">{t.date}</div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:14px" set:html={t.execP}></p>
      </div>
      <div class="ring-wrap">
        <div class="ring">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 208 208" width="200" height="200">
            <circle cx="104" cy="104" r={R} fill="none" stroke="#3D372F" stroke-width="13"/>
            <circle cx="104" cy="104" r={R} fill="none" stroke={B.hex} stroke-width="13" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray={`${dash} ${C}`} />
          </svg>
          <div class="ring-num"><span class="n" style={`color:${B.hex}`}>{SCORE}</span><span class="of">/ 100</span></div>
        </div>
        <span class={`band ${B.cls}`}>{t.band}</span>
        <span class="mono faint" style="font-size:10.5px">{t.bandR}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 0 · HNDL, apertura conceptual: lo primero que el lector entiende, antes del score -->
    <div class="rep-section hndl-open">
      <div class="eyebrow crit">{t.hndlEye}</div>
      <h2 class="hndl-h">{t.hndlH}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead" set:html={t.hndlP1}></p>
      <p class="rep-lead" set:html={t.hndlP2}></p>
      <p class="hndl-caveat">{t.hndlCaveat}</p>
      <div class="hndl-seq">
        {t.hndlSeq.map(([n, h, d], i) => (
          <div class={`st ${i === 0 ? 'now' : ''}`}>
            <span class="n">{n}</span><h3>{h}</h3><p>{d}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="hndl-bridge"><b>{t.hndlBridge}</b></p>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.hndlSrc}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1 bis · abstract de una pagina: 3 numeros + posicion vs sector + 3 acciones -->
    <div class="rep-section abstract">
      <h3>{t.absNum}</h3>
      <div class="abs-kpis">
        {t.absKpi.map(([n, k, sub]) => (
          <div class="abs-kpi"><span class="n">{n}</span><span class="k">{k}</span><span class="sub">{sub}</span></div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h3>{t.absPos}</h3>
      <div class="peer">
        <div class="peer-scale">
          <div class="peer-band" style={`left:${PARES.p25}%;width:${PARES.p75 - PARES.p25}%`}></div>
          <div class="peer-med" style={`left:${PARES.mediana}%`}></div>
          <div class="peer-you" style={`left:${SCORE}%`}></div>
        </div>
        <div class="peer-legend">
          <span><i class="sw you"></i>{es?'Usted':'You'} · {SCORE}</span>
          <span><i class="sw med"></i>{es?`Mediana de ${PARES.sector.toLowerCase()}`:`${PARES.sector} median`} · {PARES.mediana}</span>
          <span><i class="sw band"></i>{es?'Mitad central del sector':'Sector middle half'} · {PARES.p25}–{PARES.p75}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="rep-note"><strong>{t.absReal}</strong></p>
        <p class="rep-note">{es
          ? `Su puntaje queda por debajo del mínimo que medimos en la banca chilena (${PARES.min}). De las ${PARES.n} organizaciones de banca con índice calculado, ninguna está tan abajo. En soporte de intercambio híbrido el sector va en ${PARES.hibridoSector} % (n = ${PARES.hibridoN}); usted lo tiene en 2 de sus 5 hosts, y en los dos por defecto de su CDN, no por una decisión propia.`
          : `Your score falls below the minimum we measured in Chilean banking (${PARES.min}). Of the ${PARES.n} banking organizations with a computed index, none sits this low. On hybrid key exchange support the sector runs at ${PARES.hibridoSector} % (n = ${PARES.hibridoN}); you have it on 2 of your 5 hosts, and on both by CDN default rather than by your own decision.`}</p>
      </div>

      <h3>{t.absAcc}</h3>
      <ol class="abs-acc">
        {t.rm[0][2].slice(0, 2).concat([t.rm[1][2][0]]).map(([acc, esf, cost]) => (
          <li>{acc} <span class="mono faint">· {esf} · {cost}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- El Runway: score + sector + tiempo en un solo objeto -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.rwH}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.rwSub}</p>
      <div class="runway">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 900 430" role="img" aria-label={t.rwH}>
          {ZONAS.map((z, i) => {
            const xi = rwX(i === 0 ? 0 : ZONAS[i - 1].a - HOY);
            const xf = rwX(z.a - HOY);
            return (
              <g>
                <rect x={xi} y={RW.y0} width={xf - xi} height={RW.y1 - RW.y0}
                      fill="var(--crit)" opacity={z.op} />
                <line x1={xf} y1={RW.y0} x2={xf} y2={RW.y1} stroke="var(--crit)"
                      stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 4" opacity=".55" />
                <text x={xf - 6} y={RW.y0 + 14} text-anchor="end" class="mono"
                      font-size="11" fill="var(--crit)" opacity=".9">{es ? z.es : z.en}</text>
              </g>
            );
          })}

          {BANDAS_RW.map((b: any) => (
            <g>
              <line x1={RW.x0} y1={rwY(b.max)} x2={RW.x1} y2={rwY(b.max)}
                    stroke="var(--stone-line)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 5" opacity=".6" />
              <text x={RW.x0 - 12} y={rwY(b.max) + 13} text-anchor="end" font-size="12"
                    fill="var(--papyrus-dim)">{b.n}</text>
            </g>
          ))}

          {/* La banda del sector es GENUINAMENTE angosta -- banca va de 56 a 58, dos
              puntos. No se ensancha para que se vea mejor: se le pone borde para que
              se lea como banda, y la etiqueta dice su rango real. */}
          <rect x={RW.x0} y={rwY(PARES.p75)} width={RW.x1 - RW.x0} height={rwY(PARES.p25) - rwY(PARES.p75)}
                fill="var(--faience)" opacity=".18" stroke="var(--faience)" stroke-width=".75" stroke-opacity=".5" />
          <text x={RW.x0 + 8} y={rwY(PARES.p75) - 6} class="mono" font-size="10.5"
                fill="var(--faience)" opacity=".85">{t.rwSector} · {PARES.p25}–{PARES.p75}</text>
          <line x1={RW.x0} y1={rwY(PARES.mediana)} x2={RW.x1} y2={rwY(PARES.mediana)}
                stroke="var(--faience)" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <text x={RW.x1 - 4} y={rwY(PARES.mediana) - 7} text-anchor="end" class="mono"
                font-size="11" fill="var(--faience)">{t.rwMed} · {PARES.mediana}</text>

          <line x1={RW.x0} y1={RW.y0} x2={RW.x0} y2={RW.y1} stroke="var(--papyrus-dim)" stroke-width="1" />
          <circle cx={RW.x0} cy={rwY(SCORE)} r="7" fill="var(--crit)" />
          <text x={RW.x0 + 16} y={rwY(SCORE) + 4} font-size="13" fill="var(--papyrus)">
            {t.rwYou}: {SCORE}/100
          </text>

          {/* 30d, 90d y 365d ocupan 48 px de 730 en un eje de 15 anios: dibujados como
              marcas separadas se encaraman y no se leen. Van como UN corchete con su
              rango dicho en la etiqueta. */}
          <g>
            <path d={`M ${RW.x0} ${RW.y1 + 6} L ${RW.x0} ${RW.y1 + 12} L ${rwX(1)} ${RW.y1 + 12} L ${rwX(1)} ${RW.y1 + 6}`}
                  fill="none" stroke="var(--faience)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x={rwX(1) + 8} y={RW.y1 + 16} class="mono" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--faience)">
              {t.rwHitos}
            </text>
          </g>
          <text x={RW.x0} y={RW.y1 + 40} class="mono" font-size="11" fill="var(--papyrus-dim)">{t.rwHoy} · {PARES.escaneo.slice(-10)}</text>
          <text x={RW.x1} y={RW.y1 + 40} text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="11" fill="var(--papyrus-dim)">{t.rwFin}</text>
          
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="rep-note" set:html={t.rwCap}></p>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.rwSrc}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.top5}</h2>
      <ul class="top5">
        {t.findings.map(([sv, txt]) => (
          <li><span class={`sev ${sevClass(sv)}`}>{sv}</span><span>{txt}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="honesty" style="margin-top:18px"><p><b class="gold">{t.costH}.</b> <span set:html={t.cost}></span></p>
        <p class="rep-note" style="margin:.6em 0 0">{t.costPie}</p></div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2 · education -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s2}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead" set:html={t.edu}></p>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.eduPie}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2 bis · los cuatro relojes -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s2b}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.relP}</p>
      <ul class="top5">
        {t.rel.map(([n, sev, txt]) => (
          <li><span class={`sev ${sev === 'crit' ? 'critical' : 'high'}`}>{sev === 'crit' ? (es ? 'Ya corre' : 'Running') : (es ? 'Se acerca' : 'Approaching')}</span>
            <span><b>{n}.</b> {txt}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="honesty" style="margin-top:16px"><p><b class="gold">{t.chileH}.</b> <span set:html={t.chileP}></span></p></div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:26px">{t.regH}</h3>
      <table class="invtbl">
        <thead><tr>{t.regCols.map((c: string) => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>{JUR.normas.map((n: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{n.n}{!n.verificado && <span class="gold" style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px"> · por verificar</span>}</td>
            <td>{es ? n.es : n.en}</td>
            <td><span class="ok" style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace">{n.pqc ? (es ? 'Sí' : 'Yes') : 'No'}</span></td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.regJur}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 · good -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2 class="faience">{t.s3}</h2>
      <ul class="top5">{t.good.map(g => <li><span class="sev low">ok</span><span>{g}</span></li>)}</ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 4 · wrong -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s4}</h2>
      <div class="findtbl">
        <div class="findrow h"><div>{t.sev}</div><div>{t.findingCol}</div><div class="hide-m">{t.detailCol}</div></div>
        {t.sevtbl.map(([sv, f, d]) => (
          <div class="findrow"><div><span class={`sev ${sevClass(sv)}`}>{sv}</span></div><div>{f}</div><div class="hide-m muted">{d}</div></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5 · inventory -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s5}</h2>
      <table class="invtbl">
        <thead><tr>{t.invcols.map(c => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>{t.inv.map(r => (
          <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td class={r[2]==='No'?'':'ok'}><span class={r[2]==='No'?'bad':'ok'}>{r[2]}</span></td><td>{r[3]}</td></tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- 5 bis · inteligencia de proveedores: lo detectado, la biblioteca y las trampas -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s5b}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.provP}</p>

      <div class="anchor-stat">
        <div class="half"><span class="v bad">{t.anclaA}</span><span class="l">{t.anclaAL}</span></div>
        <div class="half"><span class="v ok">{t.anclaB}</span><span class="l">{t.anclaBL}</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="rep-lead" set:html={t.anclaNota}></p>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.anclaSrc}</p>

      <div class="part-h"><span class="tag2 p1">{t.p1Tag}</span><h3>{t.p1H}</h3></div>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.p1Sub}</p>
      {t.p1.map(([h, d]) => (
        <div class="cross-box"><b>{h}</b><p>{d}</p></div>
      ))}

      <div class="part-h"><span class="tag2 p2">{t.p2Tag}</span><h3>{t.p2H}</h3></div>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.p2Sub}</p>

      {GRUPOS.map((g: any) => (
        <div>
          <p class="vgroup-h">{es ? g.t.es : g.t.en}</p>
          <table class="invtbl">
            {g.dosTramos ? (
              <>
                <thead><tr>{(es ? g.cols.es : g.cols.en).map((c: string) => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
                <tbody>{g.dosTramos.map((r: any) => (
                  <tr><td>{r.p}</td>
                    <td><span class={r.sev === 'ok' ? 'ok' : r.sev === 'crit' ? 'bad' : 'gold'}>{es ? r.c.es : r.c.en}</span></td>
                    <td><span class={r.sev === 'ok' ? 'ok' : r.sev === 'crit' ? 'bad' : 'gold'}>{es ? r.o.es : r.o.en}</span></td></tr>
                ))}</tbody>
              </>
            ) : (
              <>
                <thead><tr><th>{es ? 'Proveedor · producto' : 'Vendor · product'}</th><th>{es ? 'Qué le toca' : 'What you must do'}</th><th>{es ? 'Detalle' : 'Detail'}</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>{g.filas.map((r: any) => {
                  const a = ACCION[r.a];
                  return (
                    <tr><td>{r.p}</td>
                      <td style="white-space:nowrap"><span class={a.sev === 'ok' ? 'ok' : a.sev === 'crit' ? 'bad' : 'gold'}>{es ? a.es : a.en}</span></td>
                      <td>{es ? r.es : r.en}</td></tr>
                  );
                })}</tbody>
              </>
            )}
          </table>
        </div>
      ))}

      <div class="word-trap">
        <p class="t">{t.trampasH}</p>
        {TRAMPAS.map((x: any) => (
          <p class="row"><b>{x.p}</b> — {es ? x.es : x.en}</p>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="rep-note">{t.provNota}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 6 · HNDL scenarios -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s6}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.hndlP}</p>
      <table class="invtbl">
        <thead><tr><th>{es?'Si la amenaza llega en':'If the threat arrives in'}</th><th>{es?'Probabilidad':'Probability'}</th><th>{es?'Qué significa para usted':'What it means for you'}</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{t.scen.map(([n, prob, v, c]) => (
          <tr><td>{n}</td>
            <td><span class={c==='crit'?'bad':(c==='ok'?'ok':'')} style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace">{prob}</span></td>
            <td>{v}</td></tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="rep-note">{t.scenFuente}</p>
      <p class="rep-note">{es?'Límites de la fuente: ':'Source limits: '}{t.scenAdv}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 7 · score breakdown + bands -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s7}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.scoreP}</p>
      <table class="invtbl">
        <thead><tr><th>{es?'Dimensión':'Dimension'}</th><th>{es?'Peso':'Weight'}</th><th>0–100</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{t.dims.map(d => <tr><td>{d[0]}</td><td>{d[1]}</td><td><span class={+d[2]<30?'bad':(+d[2]<50?'':'ok')}>{d[2]}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="bands-legend">{t.bands.map(b => <span class="b" style={b.activa?`color:${b.hex};border-color:${b.hex}`:''}>{b.txt}</span>)}</div>
    </div>

    <!-- 8 · roadmap -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s8}</h2>
      {t.rm.map(([hd, sub, items]) => (
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 2px"><span class="gold" style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace">{hd}</span> · {sub}</h3>
          <table class="invtbl">
            <thead><tr><th>{t.rmCols[0]}</th><th>{t.rmCols[1]}</th><th>{t.rmCols[2]}</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{items.map(([acc, esf, cost]) => (
              <tr><td>{acc}</td>
                <td style="white-space:nowrap;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace">{esf}</td>
                <td style="white-space:nowrap"><span class={/presupuesto|budget|contrato|contract|suscrip|subscri/.test(cost) ? 'gold' : 'ok'}>{cost}</span></td></tr>
            ))}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      ))}
      <p class="rep-note">{t.rmNota}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 9 · gaps / upsell -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s9}</h2>
      <div class="upsell">
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:10px">{t.gapP}</p>
        <ul class="top5">{t.gaps.map(g => <li><span class="sev info">gap</span><span>{g}</span></li>)}</ul>
        <a class="mono faience" style="display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;font-size:13px" href={p('/q-ready/checkout') + '?tier=l2'}>{t.gapCta}</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 10 · appendix -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s10}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.method}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 11 · seal -->
    <div class="rep-section">
      <h2>{t.s11}</h2>
      <p class="rep-lead">{t.sealP}</p>
      <div class="seal">content_hash = <span class="h">sha256:9f2c1a7e…d40b</span><br/>rosettaq-archive/v2 · <span class="faint">sample · not anchored</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>

<script is:inline>
  (function(){ var b=document.getElementById('qr-print'); if(b) b.addEventListener('click', function(){ window.print(); }); })();
</script>

<style>
/* Abstract de una pagina: lo que el comprador imprime y lleva a pedir presupuesto. */
.abstract{border:1px solid var(--stone-line);border-radius:4px;padding:20px 22px;margin-bottom:22px}
.abs-kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:18px;margin-bottom:20px}
.abs-kpi{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px}
.abs-kpi .n{font-size:2.1rem;line-height:1;font-family:'Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif}
.abs-kpi .k{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.75}
.abs-kpi .sub{font-size:.78rem;opacity:.62;line-height:1.35}
/* La escala de pares es 0-100 y las marcas se posicionan en %, asi que el
   contenedor tiene que sujetarlas: sin position:relative se anclan a un ancestro
   lejano y cruzan la pagina. Lo vigila check-informe-geometria.mjs. */
.peer-scale{position:relative;height:26px;border-radius:3px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  border:1px solid var(--stone-line);margin:10px 0 12px;overflow:hidden}
.peer-band{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;background:rgba(217,184,122,.22)}
.peer-med{position:absolute;top:-2px;bottom:-2px;width:2px;background:var(--gold)}
.peer-you{position:absolute;top:-2px;bottom:-2px;width:3px;background:var(--crit)}
.peer-legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 20px;font-size:.76rem;opacity:.8}
.peer-legend .sw{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px;vertical-align:-1px}
.peer-legend .sw.you{background:var(--crit)} .peer-legend .sw.med{background:var(--gold)}
.peer-legend .sw.band{background:rgba(217,184,122,.35)}

/* Las tablas de este informe son anchas por naturaleza (accion / esfuerzo / costo,
   proveedor / estado / que significa). Sin un contenedor que las haga scrollear,
   empujaban la pagina a 434 px en un telefono de 375. Se hace scrollear la tabla
   misma: no hay envoltorio que agregar en cada uso. (2026-08-21) */
.invtbl{display:block;overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%}
.invtbl thead,.invtbl tbody{display:table;width:100%;min-width:340px}
.abs-acc{margin:.4em 0 0;padding-left:1.2em} .abs-acc li{margin-bottom:.35em}
</style>

<style>
/* Apertura HNDL: cambia la jerarquia del documento — es lo primero que el lector
   entiende, antes del score. Por eso lleva marco propio y color de alerta. */
.hndl-open{border:1px solid var(--crit);border-radius:6px;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(224,112,92,.07),rgba(224,112,92,.02));
  padding:30px 30px 26px;margin-bottom:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--crit)}
.hndl-open .eyebrow.crit{color:var(--crit)}
.hndl-h{font-size:1.5rem;max-width:24ch;margin:0 0 14px}
.hndl-caveat{font-size:.83rem;opacity:.7;font-style:italic;max-width:66ch;margin:12px 0 20px}
.hndl-seq{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--stone-line);
  border:1px solid var(--stone-line);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}
@media(max-width:760px){.hndl-seq{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
.hndl-seq .st{background:var(--basalt-3,#100E0B);padding:15px 14px}
.hndl-seq .st.now{background:rgba(224,112,92,.09)}
.hndl-seq .st .n{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--crit);letter-spacing:.08em}
.hndl-seq .st h3{font-size:.92rem;margin:7px 0 6px}
.hndl-seq .st p{font-size:.78rem;opacity:.8;margin:0}
.hndl-bridge{margin-top:18px;padding-top:15px;border-top:1px dotted var(--stone-line);font-size:.88rem}

/* Ancla: dos cifras enfrentadas. El borde ya resolvio esto; el origen no. */
.anchor-stat{display:flex;border:1px solid var(--gold);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;margin:18px 0 14px}
@media(max-width:620px){.anchor-stat{flex-direction:column}}
.anchor-stat .half{flex:1;padding:18px 20px}
.anchor-stat .half:first-child{border-right:1px solid var(--stone-line)}
@media(max-width:620px){.anchor-stat .half:first-child{border-right:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--stone-line)}}
.anchor-stat .v{font-family:'Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif;font-size:2rem;display:block;line-height:1}
.anchor-stat .l{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.05em;opacity:.8;margin-top:5px;display:block;line-height:1.4}

/* Parte 1 / Parte 2: separa lo detectado en SU superficie de la biblioteca general. */
.part-h{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:28px 0 6px}
.part-h .tag2{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:2px;flex:none}
.part-h .tag2.p1{color:var(--faience);border:1px solid var(--faience)}
.part-h .tag2.p2{border:1px solid var(--stone-line);opacity:.75}
.part-h h3{margin:0}
.cross-box{border-left:2px solid var(--faience);background:rgba(77,196,181,.05);
  padding:14px 18px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;margin-bottom:10px}
.cross-box b{display:block;margin-bottom:5px}
.cross-box p{margin:0;font-size:.87rem;opacity:.85}
.vgroup-h{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin:22px 0 8px}

/* Trampas de palabras: el mismo hallazgo dicho de forma que suena a lo contrario. */
.word-trap{border:1px dashed var(--gold);border-radius:4px;padding:16px 18px;margin-top:20px}
.word-trap .t{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin:0 0 10px}
.word-trap .row{font-size:.84rem;opacity:.88;margin:0 0 9px}
.word-trap .row:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
</style>

<style>
/* El Runway. `overflow-x:auto` porque a 375 px el grafico no encoge sin volverse
   ilegible: scrollea dentro de su caja en vez de empujar la pagina. */
.runway{border:1px solid var(--stone-line);border-radius:6px;padding:20px 22px 14px;
  margin-top:10px;overflow-x:auto}
.runway svg{width:100%;min-width:640px;height:auto;display:block}
.runway svg text{font-family:-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif}
.runway svg text.mono{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',ui-monospace,monospace}
</style>
